# Order of Operations: TRANSFORM fires before DIRECTIONAL (statusblock LEFT/UP/RIGHT/DOWN).
# Wiki: object transformations (IS) happen before statusblock().
# A newly transformed object must have DIRECTIONAL applied to it in the same tick.
#
# Rock at (5,5) facing right. ROCK IS BABA transforms it to baba this tick.
# BABA IS LEFT means all baba objects face left (DIRECTIONAL sets facing).
# BABA FACING FLAG IS WIN: flag at (4,5), one tile to the left.
# BABA IS YOU: required for check_win.
#
# Correct order (TRANSFORM then DIRECTIONAL):
#   TRANSFORM: rock → baba at (5,5) facing right.
#   DIRECTIONAL: newly transformed baba has LEFT (via BABA IS LEFT) → facing = LEFT.
#   CHECK_WIN: baba at (5,5) facing left, flag at (4,5) → WON.
#
# Wrong order (DIRECTIONAL then TRANSFORM — would be the bug):
#   DIRECTIONAL: only rock exists — no ROCK IS LEFT rule → no facing change.
#   TRANSFORM: rock → baba at (5,5) facing right.
#   CHECK_WIN: baba facing right, flag at (4,5) is to the LEFT → NOT WON. Test FAILS.

[setup]
version 1
name "oop: transform before directional (newly transformed object gets facing set)"

text 0 0 rock
text 1 0 is
text 2 0 baba

text 0 1 baba
text 1 1 is
text 2 1 you

text 0 2 baba
text 1 2 is
text 2 2 left

text 0 3 baba
text 1 3 facing
text 2 3 flag
text 3 3 is
text 4 3 win

object 5 5 rock right
object 4 5 flag right

[inputs]
wait

[expected]
at 5 5 baba
not_at 5 5 rock
won
